# Normalize .gitignore
# Ignore everything in the gitignore template above, but don't ignore the .gitignore itself
!.gitignore

# Ignore the sql directory if it contains sensitive data? But we want to track the schema.
# However, note: the sql directory contains the schema and implementation guide, which we want to track.
# So we do NOT ignore the sql directory.

# We do want to ignore any local database files if they were to be generated, but we don't have any.
# If we were to have a local SQLite database for development, we would ignore it, but we are using MySQL.
# So we don't ignore .sqlite3 or similar.

# We do want to ignore any environment-specific configuration files that might contain secrets.
# We already have .env and .env.* above.

# We do not want to ignore the documentation or source code.